# The script `mise run ffi-test` has the editor's headless mode run against
# the config in `config/`, which binds no key under `C-w`, so insert state's
# `C-w` is Vim's word delete. What it prints must be exactly `expected`. It
# touches no file.

reload
settle
resize 640 480

# `i` begins an insert, `hello world` is typed, and `C-w` deletes the word
# before the bar: `hello ` is left, in insert state.
key i KeyI -
commit hello world
key w KeyW control
scene

# `l` is a key that prints, and it is text: `C-w` was no prefix.
key l KeyL -
scene
